{"$schema": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/guitaripod/wwdc-sessions/master/schema/transcript.schema.json", "id": "wwdc2019-509", "language": "eng", "source": "https://developer.apple.com/videos/play/wwdc2019/509", "wordCount": 775, "segments": [{"start": 7.0, "text": "Hello everyone, and welcome"}, {"start": 9.0, "text": "to our session about user preset"}, {"start": 11.0, "text": "support for audio units."}, {"start": 13.0, "text": "My name is Bela Balazs, and I'm"}, {"start": 14.0, "text": "an engineer on the Core Audio"}, {"start": 16.0, "text": "software team."}, {"start": 17.0, "text": "Today we would like to talk"}, {"start": 18.0, "text": "about a some of our new APIs"}, {"start": 19.0, "text": "regarding the handling of audio"}, {"start": 21.0, "text": "unit presets."}, {"start": 24.0, "text": "First, let's start with this."}, {"start": 25.0, "text": "What are presets and why are"}, {"start": 27.0, "text": "they useful?"}, {"start": 29.0, "text": "In an audio software context, a"}, {"start": 31.0, "text": "preset is a snapshot of the"}, {"start": 32.0, "text": "state of the audio unit's"}, {"start": 33.0, "text": "parameters at a given time."}, {"start": 36.0, "text": "This snapshot can be saved and"}, {"start": 38.0, "text": "later restored."}, {"start": 41.0, "text": "We already support factory"}, {"start": 42.0, "text": "presets."}, {"start": 43.0, "text": "It's a property on the AU audio"}, {"start": 45.0, "text": "unit class and it's defined as"}, {"start": 48.0, "text": "an array of AU audio unit"}, {"start": 49.0, "text": "presets."}, {"start": 50.0, "text": "These factory presets are built"}, {"start": 54.0, "text": "into the audio unit by the audio"}, {"start": 55.0, "text": "unit manufacturer."}, {"start": 57.0, "text": "An audio unit developer might"}, {"start": 59.0, "text": "include a fixed number of"}, {"start": 60.0, "text": "presets with the product as a"}, {"start": 62.0, "text": "starting point or to showcase"}, {"start": 63.0, "text": "the capabilities of the audio"}, {"start": 65.0, "text": "unit."}, {"start": 67.0, "text": "Now we are adding support for"}, {"start": 69.0, "text": "user presets."}, {"start": 70.0, "text": "These can be accessed by using"}, {"start": 72.0, "text": "this new user presets property"}, {"start": 75.0, "text": "which returns an array of AU"}, {"start": 76.0, "text": "audio unit presets."}, {"start": 79.0, "text": "These are presets that are"}, {"start": 81.0, "text": "created by the user and can be"}, {"start": 82.0, "text": "modified later on."}, {"start": 84.0, "text": "The audio unit exposes them to"}, {"start": 86.0, "text": "all audio unit host"}, {"start": 87.0, "text": "applications."}, {"start": 88.0, "text": "We have a new property called"}, {"start": 91.0, "text": "support user presets."}, {"start": 93.0, "text": "The audio unit sets this to true"}, {"start": 95.0, "text": "to signal support."}, {"start": 96.0, "text": "The audio unit host application"}, {"start": 99.0, "text": "has to check it before using the"}, {"start": 100.0, "text": "new functionality."}, {"start": 101.0, "text": "This is the way to opt in to use"}, {"start": 103.0, "text": "the new features."}, {"start": 106.0, "text": "We have methods to save and"}, {"start": 108.0, "text": "delete user presets."}, {"start": 110.0, "text": "The audio unit host application"}, {"start": 111.0, "text": "can call the save user preset"}, {"start": 113.0, "text": "method to save the current state"}, {"start": 115.0, "text": "into a preset, or it can call"}, {"start": 117.0, "text": "the delete user preset method to"}, {"start": 119.0, "text": "delete an existing preset."}, {"start": 121.0, "text": "The audio unit can override"}, {"start": 122.0, "text": "these to implement custom logic,"}, {"start": 124.0, "text": "or it can use the default"}, {"start": 125.0, "text": "implementations inherited from"}, {"start": 127.0, "text": "the AU audio unit base class."}, {"start": 131.0, "text": "These default implementations"}, {"start": 133.0, "text": "store the presets in the"}, {"start": 134.0, "text": "application container folder of"}, {"start": 135.0, "text": "the audio unit extension."}, {"start": 140.0, "text": "You can use the preset state for"}, {"start": 141.0, "text": "user preset method to retrieve"}, {"start": 143.0, "text": "the state stored in the user"}, {"start": 145.0, "text": "preset."}, {"start": 146.0, "text": "This also has a default"}, {"start": 148.0, "text": "implementation that's"}, {"start": 149.0, "text": "superclass, but it can be"}, {"start": 151.0, "text": "overridden to suit custom needs."}, {"start": 154.0, "text": "It returns a dictionary that you"}, {"start": 155.0, "text": "can use to restore the state of"}, {"start": 157.0, "text": "the audio unit by simply"}, {"start": 158.0, "text": "assigning it to the full state"}, {"start": 160.0, "text": "for document property of the"}, {"start": 161.0, "text": "audio unit."}, {"start": 164.0, "text": "In addition to these, we've"}, {"start": 166.0, "text": "added a new property called"}, {"start": 168.0, "text": "isLoadedInProcess that you can"}, {"start": 171.0, "text": "use to check whether the audio"}, {"start": 172.0, "text": "unit is loaded-in process."}, {"start": 175.0, "text": "Loading in process is a macOS"}, {"start": 177.0, "text": "only feature."}, {"start": 178.0, "text": "The host can request it but if"}, {"start": 180.0, "text": "the audio unit is not packaged"}, {"start": 181.0, "text": "to support it, the fallback"}, {"start": 183.0, "text": "behavior is to load the audio"}, {"start": 185.0, "text": "unit out of process."}, {"start": 187.0, "text": "Now, the host or the audio unit"}, {"start": 189.0, "text": "can use this property to verify"}, {"start": 191.0, "text": "that this operation succeeded."}, {"start": 193.0, "text": "And now let's see it in action."}, {"start": 198.0, "text": "So, here I have the updated AUV"}, {"start": 200.0, "text": "free host sample code, which is"}, {"start": 202.0, "text": "available both on macOS and on"}, {"start": 204.0, "text": "iOS."}, {"start": 205.0, "text": "In this host application, I have"}, {"start": 207.0, "text": "loaded the AUV free filter demo."}, {"start": 210.0, "text": "When I press play, we can hear"}, {"start": 212.0, "text": "the filter in action."}, {"start": 216.0, "text": "I can drag this graph to set the"}, {"start": 218.0, "text": "cutoff and the resonance of the"}, {"start": 220.0, "text": "filter."}, {"start": 222.0, "text": "And here I have my preset"}, {"start": 225.0, "text": "section on the right side."}, {"start": 227.0, "text": "We have our factory presets,"}, {"start": 229.0, "text": "which came with the audio unit."}, {"start": 232.0, "text": "We have warm, bright, and"}, {"start": 235.0, "text": "prominent."}, {"start": 237.0, "text": "And in the other tab, we have"}, {"start": 239.0, "text": "the user preset section."}, {"start": 242.0, "text": "Here we have my previously saved"}, {"start": 244.0, "text": "initial preset and I can save"}, {"start": 247.0, "text": "new ones."}, {"start": 258.0, "text": "And I can switch between them."}, {"start": 261.0, "text": "Once I no longer need one of the"}, {"start": 263.0, "text": "presets, I can simply delete it."}, {"start": 268.0, "text": "And this is the entire"}, {"start": 269.0, "text": "functionality of the AUV free"}, {"start": 271.0, "text": "host. I encourage everyone to check it"}, {"start": 272.0, "text": "out."}, {"start": 276.0, "text": "To summarize, we've added"}, {"start": 278.0, "text": "support for user presets for"}, {"start": 279.0, "text": "audio units to complement the"}, {"start": 281.0, "text": "functionality already provided"}, {"start": 283.0, "text": "by factory presets."}, {"start": 285.0, "text": "These allow the user to save"}, {"start": 286.0, "text": "their favorite sounds into"}, {"start": 288.0, "text": "presets and access them in each"}, {"start": 290.0, "text": "and every audio unit host"}, {"start": 291.0, "text": "application."}, {"start": 293.0, "text": "To take advantage of these new"}, {"start": 294.0, "text": "features, the audio unit can"}, {"start": 296.0, "text": "simply opt in and use the"}, {"start": 297.0, "text": "default implementations that we"}, {"start": 299.0, "text": "provide, or it can override the"}, {"start": 301.0, "text": "methods to implement custom"}, {"start": 302.0, "text": "functionality."}, {"start": 303.0, "text": "The audio unit host application"}, {"start": 305.0, "text": "can query the audio unit for"}, {"start": 307.0, "text": "these presets and can create new"}, {"start": 309.0, "text": "presets or delete the existing"}, {"start": 311.0, "text": "ones by calling the right"}, {"start": 312.0, "text": "methods on the audio unit."}, {"start": 315.0, "text": "For more information, you can"}, {"start": 316.0, "text": "check out our newly updated"}, {"start": 318.0, "text": "sample code and the resources"}, {"start": 319.0, "text": "attached to this session, which"}, {"start": 321.0, "text": "is available at developer.apple.com."}, {"start": 324.0, "text": "That concludes our presentation."}]}
